IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Part 12, Division 5 (ss 236A to 236L) and Division 6 s 237: attributed liability of corporations, partnerships, limited liability partnerships and officers.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Generated from work/gen/gen_attributed.py so that the three families (236B-236D corporation, 236E-236G partnership or
-- limited liability partnership, 236H-236I officer, partner or manager) read alike. Markers are explained at the head of sfab-division-1.l4 and sfab-civil.l4.
-- Section 236A's "defendant", "defendant corporation" and "defendant partnership" are defined terms; later sections take their answers as inputs.

§ `s 236A: interpretation of this Division`

-- src:36304 | 236A. In this Division, unless the context otherwise requires —
@ref s 236A (src:36304-36304)
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H in respect of a contravention of a provision of Part 12 committed by a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual who is liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H in respect of a contravention of any provision in Part 12 committed by a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236A "defendant" an individual liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H` MEANS
    IF `the person is an individual liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H in respect of a contravention of a provision of Part 12 committed by a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“defendant” means an individual liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H"

-- src:36306 | “defendant” means an individual liable to an order for a civil
-- src:36307 | penalty under section 236H in respect of a contravention of
-- src:36308 | any provision in this Part committed by a corporation,
-- src:36309 | partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated
-- src:36310 | association;
@ref s 236A (src:36306-36310)
GIVEN
    `the corporation is liable to be punished under section 236B(1) or to an order for a civil penalty under section 236B(3) in respect of a contravention committed by its employee or officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation liable to be punished under section 236B(1), or to an order for a civil penalty under section 236B(3), in respect of a contravention of any provision in Part 12 committed by its employee or officer?
    `the corporation is liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the corporation liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236C(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236A "defendant corporation" a corporation liable under section 236B or 236C` MEANS
    IF `the corporation is liable to be punished under section 236B(1) or to an order for a civil penalty under section 236B(3) in respect of a contravention committed by its employee or officer` OR `the corporation is liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236C(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“defendant corporation” means a corporation"

-- src:36312 | “defendant corporation” means a corporation ––
-- src:36314 | (a) liable to be punished under section 236B(1) or to an
-- src:36315 | order for a civil penalty under section 236B(3) in
-- src:36316 | respect of a contravention of any provision in this
-- src:36317 | Part committed by its employee or officer; or
-- src:36319 | (b) liable to an order for a civil penalty under
-- src:36320 | section 236C(1);
@ref s 236A (src:36312-36320)
GIVEN
    `the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under section 236E(1) or to an order for a civil penalty under section 236E(3) in respect of a contravention committed by a partner, manager or employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the partnership or limited liability partnership liable to be punished under section 236E(1), or to an order for a civil penalty under section 236E(3), in respect of a contravention of any provision in Part 12 committed by a partner or employee of the partnership or a partner, manager or employee of the limited liability partnership, as the case may be?
    `the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236F(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the partnership or limited liability partnership liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236F(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236A "defendant partnership" a partnership or limited liability partnership liable under section 236E or 236F` MEANS
    IF `the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under section 236E(1) or to an order for a civil penalty under section 236E(3) in respect of a contravention committed by a partner, manager or employee` OR `the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236F(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“defendant partnership” means a partnership or limited liability partnership"

-- src:36322 | “defendant partnership” means a partnership or limited liability
-- src:36323 | partnership ––
-- src:36328 | (a) liable to be punished under section 236E(1) or to an
-- src:36329 | order for a civil penalty under section 236E(3) in
