§ `s 236B: liability when employee or officer commits a contravention with the consent or connivance of the corporation`

-- src:36349 | 236B.—(1) Where an offence of contravening any provision in this
-- src:36350 | Part is proved to have been committed by an employee or an officer of
-- src:36351 | a corporation (called in this section the contravening person) —
-- src:36353 | (a) with the consent or connivance of the corporation; and
-- src:36355 | (b) for the benefit of the corporation,
-- src:36357 | the corporation shall be guilty of that offence as if the corporation had
-- src:36358 | committed the contravention, and shall be liable to be proceeded
-- src:36359 | against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 236B(1) (src:36349-36359)
GIVEN
    `an offence of contravening a provision of Part 12 is proved to have been committed by an employee or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an offence of contravening any provision of Part 12 proved to have been committed by an employee or an officer of a corporation (the contravening person)?
    `the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed with the consent or connivance of the corporation?
    `the offence was committed for the benefit of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236B(1) the corporation is guilty of the offence as if it had committed the contravention` MEANS
    IF `an offence of contravening a provision of Part 12 is proved to have been committed by an employee or an officer of the corporation` AND `the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the corporation` AND `the offence was committed for the benefit of the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence of contravening any provision in this Part is proved to have been committed by an employee or an officer of a corporation" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [WHERE] -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

@ref s 236B(1) (src:36349-36359)
GIVEN
    `the penalty for the offence that the contravening person is proved to have committed` IS A Penalty @desc What is the penalty the Act provides for the offence that the contravening person is proved to have committed (the answer under the section that creates the offence)?
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 236B(1) the corporation is liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly` MEANS
    `the penalty for the offence that the contravening person is proved to have committed`  -- "shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly": the penalty of the offence itself


-- src:36363 | (2) No proceedings shall be instituted against a corporation under
-- src:36364 | subsection (1) after —
-- src:36366 | (a) a court has made an order against the corporation for the
-- src:36367 | payment of a civil penalty under subsection (3); or
-- src:36369 | (b) the corporation has entered into an agreement with the
-- src:36370 | Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a
-- src:36371 | civil penalty under section 232(5) (as that provision is
-- src:36372 | applied to an action under subsection (3) by
-- src:36373 | subsection (6)),
-- src:36378 | in respect of the same contravention.
@ref s 236B(2) (src:36363-36378)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order against the corporation for the payment of a civil penalty under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the corporation for the payment of a civil penalty under subsection (3) in respect of the same contravention?
    `the corporation has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) as applied by subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 232(5) (as that provision is applied to an action under subsection (3) by subsection (6)) in respect of the same contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236B(2) proceedings against the corporation under subsection (1) are barred` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order against the corporation for the payment of a civil penalty under subsection (3)` OR `the corporation has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) as applied by subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings shall be instituted against a corporation under subsection (1) after" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)


-- src:36382 | (3) Where it appears to the Authority that a corporation is liable to
-- src:36383 | be punished under subsection (1) for a contravention committed by a
-- src:36384 | contravening person, the Authority may, with the consent of the
-- src:36385 | Public Prosecutor, bring an action in a court against the corporation to
-- src:36386 | seek an order for a civil penalty in respect of that contravention as if
-- src:36387 | the corporation had committed the contravention, whether or not such
-- src:36388 | action is brought against the contravening person.
@ref s 236B(3) (src:36382-36388)
GIVEN
    `it appears to the Authority that the corporation is liable to be punished under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Authority that the corporation is liable to be punished under subsection (1) for a contravention committed by a contravening person?
    `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Public Prosecutor consented to the Authority bringing the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236B(3) the Authority may bring an action in a court against the corporation to seek an order for a civil penalty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it appears to the Authority that the corporation is liable to be punished under subsection (1)`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it appears to the Authority that a corporation is liable to be punished under subsection (1) for a contravention committed by a contravening person" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHERE] -- GRANT-GROUP [WHERE-LISTED]
        IF NOT `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Authority may, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action in a court against the corporation" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [CONSENT] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


-- src:36392 | (4) If the court in subsection (3) is satisfied on a balance of
-- src:36393 | probabilities that the corporation is liable to be punished under
-- src:36394 | subsection (1) for a contravention of any provision of this Part, the
-- src:36395 | court may make an order against the corporation for the payment of a
-- src:36396 | civil penalty of a sum not less than $100,000 but not exceeding the
-- src:36397 | greater of the following:
-- src:36399 | (a) 3 times —
-- src:36401 | (i) the amount of the profit that the corporation gained
-- src:36402 | as a result of the contravention by the contravening
-- src:36403 | person; or
-- src:36405 | (ii) the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as
-- src:36406 | a result of the contravention by the contravening
-- src:36407 | person;
-- src:36409 | (b) $2 million. [4/2017]
@ref s 236B(4) (src:36392-36409)
GIVEN
    `the court in subsection (3) is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the corporation is liable to be punished under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court in subsection (3) satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the corporation is liable to be punished under subsection (1) for a contravention of a provision of Part 12?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236B(4) the court may make an order against the corporation for the payment of a civil penalty` MEANS
    IF `the court in subsection (3) is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the corporation is liable to be punished under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court in subsection (3) is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the corporation is liable to be punished under subsection (1)" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [IF-NOTHING]


@ref s 236B(4) (src:36392-36409)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236B(4) the highest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (3 TIMES `the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`) GREATER THAN 2000000 AND `the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        THEN 3 TIMES `the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        IF (3 TIMES `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`) GREATER THAN 2000000
        THEN 3 TIMES `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`  -- FORK F-232-2a: "or" read as the greater of the two when both are present
        OTHERWISE 2000000  -- "not exceeding the greater of the following" (b) $2 million

@ref s 236B(4) (src:36392-36409)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236B(4) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS 100000  -- "a sum not less than $100,000"

-- s 236B(5) is shown as deleted in this text; the coverage table records it.

