    IF `the action is brought against the corporation under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply in relation to an action brought against a corporation under subsection (3)"


-- src:36418 | (7) Any defence that would be available to —
-- src:36420 | (a) the contravening person if the contravening person were
-- src:36421 | prosecuted for the contravening person’s contravention; or
-- src:36423 | (b) the corporation if it were prosecuted under subsection (1)
-- src:36424 | in respect of that contravention,
-- src:36429 | is also available to the corporation in an action under subsection (3) in
-- src:36430 | respect of that contravention.
@ref s 236B(7) (src:36418-36430)
GIVEN
    `a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the contravening person in a prosecution answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `a defence would be available to the corporation if it were prosecuted under subsection (1) in respect of that contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the corporation in a prosecution under subsection (1) answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236B(7) the defence is also available to the corporation in an action under subsection (3)` MEANS
    IF (`a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`a defence would be available to the corporation if it were prosecuted under subsection (1) in respect of that contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is also available to the corporation in an action under subsection (3)"


-- src:36434 | (8) The means by which consent or connivance of the corporation
-- src:36435 | under subsection (1) or (3) may be established include proving that —
-- src:36437 | (a) the corporation’s board of directors intentionally,
-- src:36438 | knowingly or recklessly carried out the relevant conduct,
-- src:36439 | or expressly, tacitly or impliedly authorised or permitted
-- src:36440 | the contravention;
-- src:36442 | (b) a high managerial agent of the corporation intentionally,
-- src:36443 | knowingly or recklessly engaged in the relevant conduct,
-- src:36444 | or expressly, tacitly or impliedly authorised or permitted
-- src:36445 | the contravention; or
-- src:36447 | (c) a corporate culture existed within the corporation that
-- src:36448 | directed or encouraged non‑compliance with the relevant
-- src:36449 | provision.
@ref s 236B(8) (src:36434-36449)
GIVEN
    `the board of directors of the corporation carried out or authorised the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that the corporation’s board of directors intentionally, knowingly or recklessly carried out the relevant conduct, or expressly, tacitly or impliedly authorised or permitted the contravention?
    `a high managerial agent of the corporation engaged in or authorised the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that a high managerial agent of the corporation intentionally, knowingly or recklessly engaged in the relevant conduct, or expressly, tacitly or impliedly authorised or permitted the contravention?
    `a corporate culture existed within the corporation that directed or encouraged non-compliance with the relevant provision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it proved that a corporate culture existed within the corporation that directed or encouraged non-compliance with the relevant provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236B(8) the consent or connivance of the corporation is established` MEANS
    IF `the board of directors of the corporation carried out or authorised the contravention` OR `a high managerial agent of the corporation engaged in or authorised the contravention` OR `a corporate culture existed within the corporation that directed or encouraged non-compliance with the relevant provision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The means by which consent or connivance of the corporation under subsection (1) or (3) may be established include proving that"


