    IF `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the corporation has committed a contravention under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the corporation has committed a contravention under subsection (1)" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [IF-NOTHING]


@ref s 236C(3) (src:36498-36514)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236C(3) the highest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (3 TIMES `the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`) GREATER THAN 2000000 AND `the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        THEN 3 TIMES `the amount of the profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        IF (3 TIMES `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`) GREATER THAN 2000000
        THEN 3 TIMES `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`  -- FORK F-232-2a: "or" read as the greater of the two when both are present
        OTHERWISE 2000000  -- "not exceeding the greater of the following" (b) $2 million

@ref s 236C(3) (src:36498-36514)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236C(3) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS 100000  -- "a sum not less than $100,000"

-- s 236C(4) is shown as deleted in this text; the coverage table records it.

-- src:36517 | (5) Sections 232(4) to (7) and 233 apply in relation to an action
-- src:36518 | brought against a corporation under subsection (2) as they apply in
-- src:36519 | relation to an action under section 232.
@ref s 236C(5) (src:36517-36519)
GIVEN
    `the action is brought against the corporation under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action one brought against the corporation under subsection (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236C(5) sections 232(4) to (7) and 233 apply to the action under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `the action is brought against the corporation under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply in relation to an action brought against a corporation under subsection (2)"


-- src:36523 | (6) Any defence that would be available to the contravening person
-- src:36524 | if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening
-- src:36525 | person’s contravention is also available to the corporation in an action
-- src:36530 | under subsection (2) in respect of its failure to prevent or detect that
-- src:36531 | contravention.
@ref s 236C(6) (src:36523-36531)
GIVEN
    `a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the contravening person in a prosecution answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236C(6) the defence is also available to the corporation in an action under subsection (2)` MEANS
    IF `a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is also available to the corporation in an action under subsection (2)"


-- src:36535 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining whether a
-- src:36536 | contravention is attributable to the negligence of a corporation, the
-- src:36537 | court is to take into account the following matters:
-- src:36539 | (a) whether the corporation has established adequate policies
-- src:36540 | and procedures for the purposes of preventing and
-- src:36541 | detecting market misconduct;
-- src:36543 | (b) whether the corporation has consistently enforced
-- src:36544 | compliance with its policies and procedures referred to
-- src:36545 | in paragraph (a);
-- src:36547 | (c) such other factors as the court may consider relevant.
@ref s 236C(7) (src:36535-36547)
GIVEN
    `the court is determining whether a contravention is attributable to the negligence of the corporation for the purposes of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court determining, for the purposes of subsection (1), whether a contravention is attributable to the negligence of the corporation?
    `the matter is whether the corporation has established adequate policies and procedures for the purposes of preventing and detecting market misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter whether the corporation has established adequate policies and procedures for the purposes of preventing and detecting market misconduct?
    `the matter is whether the corporation has consistently enforced compliance with its policies and procedures referred to in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter whether the corporation has consistently enforced compliance with its policies and procedures referred to in paragraph (a)?
    `the matter is another factor that the court may consider relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter another factor that the court may consider relevant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236C(7) the matter is one the court is to take into account in deciding negligence` MEANS
    IF `the court is determining whether a contravention is attributable to the negligence of the corporation for the purposes of subsection (1)` AND (`the matter is whether the corporation has established adequate policies and procedures for the purposes of preventing and detecting market misconduct` OR `the matter is whether the corporation has consistently enforced compliance with its policies and procedures referred to in paragraph (a)` OR `the matter is another factor that the court may consider relevant`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining whether a contravention is attributable to the negligence of a corporation"


§ `s 236D: civil liability of the corporation`

-- src:36554 | 236D.—(1) A defendant corporation which has gained a profit or
-- src:36555 | avoided a loss as a result of the contravention of a provision in this
-- src:36556 | Part by the contravening person referred to in section 236B(1) or
-- src:36557 | 236C(1) is, whether or not it had been convicted or had a civil penalty
-- src:36558 | imposed on it, liable to pay compensation to any person (called in this
-- src:36559 | section the claimant) who ––
-- src:36561 | (a) had been dealing in capital markets products of the same
-- src:36562 | description contemporaneously with the contravention by
-- src:36563 | the contravening person; and
-- src:36565 | (b) had suffered loss by reason of the difference between —
-- src:36567 | (i) the price at which the capital markets products were
-- src:36568 | dealt in contemporaneously with the contravention
-- src:36569 | by the contravening person; and
-- src:36571 | (ii) the price at which the capital markets products would
-- src:36572 | have been likely to have been so dealt in at the time
-- src:36573 | of the contemporaneous dealing if —
-- src:36575 | (A) in any case where the contravening person had
-- src:36576 | acted in contravention of section 218 or 219,
-- src:36581 | the information referred to in section 218(1) or
-- src:36582 | 219(1) (as the case may be) had been generally
-- src:36583 | available; or
-- src:36585 | (B) in any other case, the contravention by the
-- src:36586 | contravening person had not occurred.
@ref s 236D(1) (src:36554-36586)
GIVEN
    `the corporation is a defendant corporation (the answer under section 236A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for "defendant corporation" in section 236A answer for this corporation? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the corporation has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention of a provision of Part 12 by the contravening person?
    `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person? (the court takes the matters in section 234(5) into account)
    `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price dealt in contemporaneously and the price likely to have been so dealt in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant suffered loss by reason of the difference between (i) the price at which the capital markets products were dealt in contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person and (ii) the price at which they would have been likely to have been so dealt in, on the hypothesis that paragraph (b)(ii)(A) or (B) selects?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236D(1) the corporation is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the corporation is a defendant corporation (the answer under section 236A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A defendant corporation which has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention of a provision in this Part by the contravening person referred to in section 236B(1) or 236C(1)" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF NOT `the corporation has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b) -- GRANT-GROUP [ENTITLED]
        IF `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` AND `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price dealt in contemporaneously and the price likely to have been so dealt in`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person (called in this section the claimant) who" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

@ref s 236D(1) (src:36575-36583)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the contravening person acted in contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236D(1)(b)(ii)(A) the price to compare is the price had the information been generally available` MEANS
    IF `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any case where the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219"

@ref s 236D(1) (src:36585-36586)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the contravening person acted in contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236D(1)(b)(ii)(B) the price to compare is the price had the contravention not occurred` MEANS
    IF NOT `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any other case"


-- src:36590 | (2) The amount of compensation that the defendant corporation is
-- src:36591 | liable to pay to the claimant under subsection (1) is the amount of the
-- src:36592 | loss suffered by the claimant, after deducting any amount of
-- src:36593 | compensation paid or payable —
-- src:36595 | (a) by the contravening person under an order of court or an
-- src:36596 | agreement to pay; or
-- src:36598 | (b) under an order for disgorgement under section 236L,
-- src:36600 | to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention, up to the
-- src:36601 | maximum recoverable amount.
@ref s 236D(2) (src:36590-36601)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant?
    `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention under an order of court or an agreement to pay by the contravening person or any defendant, defendant corporation or defendant partnership under Division 4 or 5, or under an order for disgorgement under section 236L? (0 if none)
    `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 236D(6))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum recoverable amount under section 236D(6) for this contravention?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236D(2) the amount of compensation under subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` AT MOST 0
        THEN 0  -- FORK F-234-2: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing owed
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 236D(6))`
        THEN `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 236D(6))`  -- "up to the maximum recoverable amount"
        OTHERWISE `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention`


-- src:36605 | (3) Any defence that would be available to —
-- src:36607 | (a) the contravening person if the contravening person were
-- src:36608 | prosecuted for the contravening person’s contravention; or
-- src:36610 | (b) the defendant corporation if it were prosecuted under
-- src:36611 | section 236B(1) or had an action brought against it under
-- src:36612 | section 236C(2),
-- src:36614 | is also available to the defendant corporation in an action under this
-- src:36615 | section in respect of that contravention.
@ref s 236D(3) (src:36605-36615)
GIVEN
    `a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the contravening person in a prosecution answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `a defence would be available to the defendant corporation if it were prosecuted under section 236B(1) or had an action brought against it under section 236C(2) (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the defendant corporation if it were prosecuted under section 236B(1) or had an action brought against it under section 236C(2) answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236D(3) the defence is also available to the corporation in an action under this section` MEANS
    IF (`a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`a defence would be available to the defendant corporation if it were prosecuted under section 236B(1) or had an action brought against it under section 236C(2) (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is also available to the defendant corporation in an action under this section"


-- src:36619 | (4) An action under this section must not be commenced after the
-- src:36620 | expiration of 6 years from the date of completion of the
-- src:36621 | contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred.
@ref s 236D(4) (src:36619-36621)
GIVEN
    `the date of completion of the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred completed?
    `the date the action under section 236D is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action under section 236D commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236D(4) the action under section 236D is barred because 6 years have expired from the date of completion of the dealing` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of completion of the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred` `the date the action under section 236D is commenced` 6 Years
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced after the expiration of 6 years from the date of completion of the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
    ELSE JUST TRUE


-- src:36625 | (5) In determining whether the dealing took place
-- src:36626 | contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening
-- src:36627 | person, the court is to take into account the matters set out in
-- src:36628 | section 234(5).
@ref s 236D(5) (src:36625-36628)
GIVEN
    `the court is determining whether the dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court determining whether the dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236D(5) the court is to take into account the matters in section 234(5)` MEANS
    IF `the court is determining whether the dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether" "took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person"


-- src:36635 | (6) In this section, “maximum recoverable amount” means —
-- src:36637 | (a) the amount of profit that the defendant corporation gained;
-- src:36638 | or
-- src:36640 | (b) the amount of the loss that it avoided,
-- src:36642 | as a result of the contravention by the contravening person, after
-- src:36643 | deducting all amounts of compensation that the defendant
-- src:36644 | corporation had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other
-- src:36645 | claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention.
@ref s 236D(6) (src:36635-36645)
GIVEN
    `the amount of profit that the corporation gained` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of profit that the corporation gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the compensation the corporation had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation that the corporation had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236D(6) the maximum recoverable amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the amount of profit that the corporation gained` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided`) AND (`the amount of profit that the corporation gained` MINUS `the compensation the corporation had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN 0)
        THEN `the amount of profit that the corporation gained` MINUS `the compensation the corporation had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention`  -- FORK F-234-6: "(a) the profit gained; or (b) the loss avoided" read as the greater of the two when both are present
        IF (NOT (`the amount of profit that the corporation gained` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided`)) AND (`the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided` MINUS `the compensation the corporation had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN 0)
        THEN `the amount of the loss that the corporation avoided` MINUS `the compensation the corporation had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention`
        OTHERWISE 0  -- FORK F-234-6: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing recoverable

§ `s 236E: liability when partner, manager or employee commits a contravention with the consent or connivance of the partnership or limited liability partnership`

-- src:36655 | 236E.—(1) Where an offence of contravening any provision of this
-- src:36656 | Part is proved to have been committed by a partner or employee of a
-- src:36657 | partnership or a partner, manager or employee of a limited liability
-- src:36658 | partnership (called in this section the contravening person) —
-- src:36660 | (a) with the consent or connivance of the partnership or
-- src:36661 | limited liability partnership; and
-- src:36663 | (b) for the benefit of the partnership or limited liability
-- src:36664 | partnership,
-- src:36666 | the partnership or limited liability partnership shall be guilty of that
-- src:36667 | offence as if it had committed the contravention, and every partner of
-- src:36668 | that partnership, or the limited liability partnership (as the case may
-- src:36669 | be) shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 236E(1) (src:36655-36669)
GIVEN
    `an offence of contravening a provision of Part 12 is proved to have been committed by a partner or employee of the partnership, or a partner, manager or employee of the limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an offence of contravening any provision of Part 12 proved to have been committed by a partner or employee of a partnership, or a partner, manager or employee of a limited liability partnership (the contravening person)?
    `the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the partnership or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed with the consent or connivance of the partnership or limited liability partnership?
    `the offence was committed for the benefit of the partnership or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the offence committed for the benefit of the partnership or limited liability partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236E(1) the partnership or limited liability partnership is guilty of the offence as if it had committed the contravention` MEANS
    IF `an offence of contravening a provision of Part 12 is proved to have been committed by a partner or employee of the partnership, or a partner, manager or employee of the limited liability partnership` AND `the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the partnership or limited liability partnership` AND `the offence was committed for the benefit of the partnership or limited liability partnership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence of contravening any provision of this Part is proved to have been committed by a partner or employee of a partnership or a partner, manager or employee of a limited liability partnership" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [WHERE] -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

@ref s 236E(1) (src:36655-36669)
GIVEN
    `the penalty for the offence that the contravening person is proved to have committed` IS A Penalty @desc What is the penalty the Act provides for the offence that the contravening person is proved to have committed (the answer under the section that creates the offence)?
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 236E(1) the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly` MEANS
    `the penalty for the offence that the contravening person is proved to have committed`  -- "shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly": the penalty of the offence itself


-- src:36673 | (2) No proceedings shall be instituted against any partner of the
-- src:36674 | partnership or the limited liability partnership under subsection (1)
-- src:36675 | after —
-- src:36677 | (a) a court has made an order against the partner or limited
-- src:36678 | liability partnership for the payment of a civil penalty
-- src:36679 | under subsection (3); or
-- src:36684 | (b) the partner or limited liability partnership has entered into
-- src:36685 | an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without
-- src:36686 | admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 232(5)
-- src:36687 | (as that provision is applied to an action under
-- src:36688 | subsection (3) by subsection (6)),
-- src:36690 | in respect of the same contravention.
@ref s 236E(2) (src:36673-36690)
GIVEN
    `a court has made an order against the partner or the limited liability partnership for the payment of a civil penalty under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a court made an order against the partner or the limited liability partnership for the payment of a civil penalty under subsection (3) in respect of the same contravention?
    `the partner or the limited liability partnership has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) as applied by subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the partner or the limited liability partnership entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay, with or without admission of liability, a civil penalty under section 232(5) (as that provision is applied to an action under subsection (3) by subsection (6)) in respect of the same contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236E(2) proceedings against the partnership or limited liability partnership under subsection (1) are barred` MEANS
    IF `a court has made an order against the partner or the limited liability partnership for the payment of a civil penalty under subsection (3)` OR `the partner or the limited liability partnership has entered into an agreement with the Authority to pay a civil penalty under section 232(5) as applied by subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "No proceedings shall be instituted against any partner of the partnership or the limited liability partnership under subsection (1) after" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)


-- src:36694 | (3) Where it appears to the Authority that a partnership or a limited
-- src:36695 | liability partnership is liable to be punished under subsection (1) for a
-- src:36696 | contravention committed by a contravening person, the Authority
-- src:36697 | may, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action in a
-- src:36698 | court against the partnership or limited liability partnership to seek an
-- src:36699 | order for a civil penalty in respect of that contravention as if the
-- src:36700 | partnership or limited liability partnership had committed the
-- src:36701 | contravention, whether or not such action is brought against the
-- src:36702 | contravening person.
@ref s 236E(3) (src:36694-36702)
GIVEN
    `it appears to the Authority that the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Authority that the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under subsection (1) for a contravention committed by a contravening person?
    `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Public Prosecutor consented to the Authority bringing the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236E(3) the Authority may bring an action in a court against the partnership or limited liability partnership to seek an order for a civil penalty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it appears to the Authority that the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under subsection (1)`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it appears to the Authority that a partnership or a limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under subsection (1) for a contravention committed by a contravening person" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHERE] -- GRANT-GROUP [WHERE-LISTED]
        IF NOT `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Authority may, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action in a court against the partnership or limited liability partnership" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [CONSENT] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE


-- src:36706 | (4) If the court in subsection (3) is satisfied on a balance of
-- src:36707 | probabilities that the partnership or limited liability partnership is
-- src:36708 | liable to be punished under subsection (1) for a contravention of any
-- src:36709 | provision of this Part, the court may make an order against the
-- src:36710 | partnership or limited liability partnership for the payment of a civil
-- src:36711 | penalty of a sum not less than $50,000 but not exceeding the greater
-- src:36712 | of the following:
-- src:36714 | (a) 3 times —
-- src:36716 | (i) the amount of the profit that the partnership or
-- src:36717 | limited liability partnership gained as a result of the
-- src:36718 | contravention by the contravening person; or
-- src:36720 | (ii) the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited
-- src:36721 | liability partnership avoided as a result of the
-- src:36722 | contravention by the contravening person;
-- src:36724 | (b) $2 million. [4/2017]
@ref s 236E(4) (src:36706-36724)
GIVEN
    `the court in subsection (3) is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court in subsection (3) satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under subsection (1) for a contravention of a provision of Part 12?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236E(4) the court may make an order against the partnership or limited liability partnership for the payment of a civil penalty` MEANS
    IF `the court in subsection (3) is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court in subsection (3) is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to be punished under subsection (1)" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [IF-NOTHING]


@ref s 236E(4) (src:36706-36724)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236E(4) the highest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (3 TIMES `the amount of the profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`) GREATER THAN 2000000 AND `the amount of the profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        THEN 3 TIMES `the amount of the profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        IF (3 TIMES `the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`) GREATER THAN 2000000
        THEN 3 TIMES `the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`  -- FORK F-232-2a: "or" read as the greater of the two when both are present
        OTHERWISE 2000000  -- "not exceeding the greater of the following" (b) $2 million

@ref s 236E(4) (src:36706-36724)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236E(4) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS 50000  -- "a sum not less than $50,000"

