    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsection (1), in determining whether a contravention is attributable to the negligence of a partnership or limited liability partnership"


§ `s 236G: civil liability of the partnership or limited liability partnership`

-- src:36881 | 236G.—(1) A defendant partnership which has gained a profit or
-- src:36882 | avoided a loss as a result of the contravention of a provision in this
-- src:36883 | Part by the contravening person referred to in section 236E(1) or
-- src:36884 | 236F(1) is, whether or not the partners of the partnership or the
-- src:36885 | limited liability partnership had been convicted or the partnership or
-- src:36886 | limited liability partnership had a civil penalty imposed on it, liable to
-- src:36887 | pay compensation to any person (called in this section the claimant)
-- src:36888 | who —
-- src:36890 | (a) had been dealing in capital markets products of the same
-- src:36891 | description contemporaneously with the contravention by
-- src:36892 | the contravening person; and
-- src:36894 | (b) had suffered loss by reason of the difference between —
-- src:36896 | (i) the price at which the capital markets products were
-- src:36897 | dealt in contemporaneously with the contravention
-- src:36898 | by the contravening person; and
-- src:36900 | (ii) the price at which the capital markets products would
-- src:36901 | have been likely to have been so dealt in at the time
-- src:36902 | of the contemporaneous dealing if —
-- src:36904 | (A) in any case where the contravening person had
-- src:36905 | acted in contravention of section 218 or 219,
-- src:36906 | the information referred to in section 218(1) or
-- src:36907 | 219(1) (as the case may be) had been generally
-- src:36908 | available; or
-- src:36910 | (B) in any other case, the contravention by the
-- src:36911 | contravening person had not occurred.
@ref s 236G(1) (src:36881-36911)
GIVEN
    `the partnership or limited liability partnership is a defendant partnership (the answer under section 236A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for "defendant partnership" in section 236A answer for this partnership or limited liability partnership? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the partnership or limited liability partnership has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the partnership or limited liability partnership gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention of a provision of Part 12 by the contravening person?
    `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person? (the court takes the matters in section 234(5) into account)
    `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price dealt in contemporaneously and the price likely to have been so dealt in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant suffered loss by reason of the difference between (i) the price at which the capital markets products were dealt in contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person and (ii) the price at which they would have been likely to have been so dealt in, on the hypothesis that paragraph (b)(ii)(A) or (B) selects?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236G(1) the partnership or limited liability partnership is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the partnership or limited liability partnership is a defendant partnership (the answer under section 236A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A defendant partnership which has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention of a provision in this Part by the contravening person referred to in section 236E(1) or 236F(1)" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF NOT `the partnership or limited liability partnership has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "which has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b) -- GRANT-GROUP [ENTITLED]
        IF `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` AND `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price dealt in contemporaneously and the price likely to have been so dealt in`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person (called in this section the claimant) who" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

@ref s 236G(1) (src:36904-36908)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the contravening person acted in contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236G(1)(b)(ii)(A) the price to compare is the price had the information been generally available` MEANS
    IF `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any case where the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219"

@ref s 236G(1) (src:36910-36911)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the contravening person acted in contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236G(1)(b)(ii)(B) the price to compare is the price had the contravention not occurred` MEANS
    IF NOT `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any other case"


-- src:36915 | (2) The amount of compensation that the defendant partnership is
-- src:36916 | liable to pay to the claimant under subsection (1) is the amount of the
-- src:36917 | loss suffered by the claimant, after deducting any amount of
-- src:36918 | compensation paid or payable —
-- src:36920 | (a) by the contravening person under an order of court or an
-- src:36921 | agreement to pay; or
-- src:36926 | (b) under an order for disgorgement under section 236L,
-- src:36928 | to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention, up to the
-- src:36929 | maximum recoverable amount.
@ref s 236G(2) (src:36915-36929)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant?
    `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention under an order of court or an agreement to pay by the contravening person or any defendant, defendant corporation or defendant partnership under Division 4 or 5, or under an order for disgorgement under section 236L? (0 if none)
    `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 236G(6))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum recoverable amount under section 236G(6) for this contravention?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236G(2) the amount of compensation under subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` AT MOST 0
        THEN 0  -- FORK F-234-2: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing owed
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 236G(6))`
        THEN `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 236G(6))`  -- "up to the maximum recoverable amount"
        OTHERWISE `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention`


-- src:36933 | (3) Any defence that would be available to —
-- src:36935 | (a) the contravening person if the contravening person were
-- src:36936 | prosecuted for the contravening person’s contravention; or
-- src:36938 | (b) the defendant partnership if it were prosecuted under
-- src:36939 | section 236E(1) or had an action brought against it under
-- src:36940 | section 236F(2),
-- src:36942 | is also available to the defendant partnership in an action under this
-- src:36943 | section in respect of that contravention.
@ref s 236G(3) (src:36933-36943)
GIVEN
    `a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the contravening person in a prosecution answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `a defence would be available to the defendant partnership if it were prosecuted under section 236E(1) or had an action brought against it under section 236F(2) (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the defendant partnership if it were prosecuted under section 236E(1) or had an action brought against it under section 236F(2) answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236G(3) the defence is also available to the partnership or limited liability partnership in an action under this section` MEANS
    IF (`a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`a defence would be available to the defendant partnership if it were prosecuted under section 236E(1) or had an action brought against it under section 236F(2) (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is also available to the defendant partnership in an action under this section"


-- src:36947 | (4) An action under this section must not be commenced after the
-- src:36948 | expiration of 6 years from the date of completion of the
-- src:36949 | contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred.
@ref s 236G(4) (src:36947-36949)
GIVEN
    `the date of completion of the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred completed?
    `the date the action under section 236G is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action under section 236G commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236G(4) the action under section 236G is barred because 6 years have expired from the date of completion of the dealing` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of completion of the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred` `the date the action under section 236G is commenced` 6 Years
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced after the expiration of 6 years from the date of completion of the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
    ELSE JUST TRUE


-- src:36953 | (5) In determining whether the dealing took place
-- src:36954 | contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening
-- src:36955 | person, the court is to take into account the matters set out in
-- src:36956 | section 234(5).
@ref s 236G(5) (src:36953-36956)
GIVEN
    `the court is determining whether the dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court determining whether the dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236G(5) the court is to take into account the matters in section 234(5)` MEANS
    IF `the court is determining whether the dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether" "took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person"


-- src:36960 | (6) In this section, “maximum recoverable amount” means —
-- src:36962 | (a) the amount of profit that the defendant partnership gained;
-- src:36963 | or
-- src:36965 | (b) the amount of the loss that it avoided,
-- src:36967 | as a result of the contravention by the contravening person, after
-- src:36968 | deducting all amounts of compensation that the defendant partnership
-- src:36969 | had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants
-- src:36970 | under this section in respect of the same contravention.
@ref s 236G(6) (src:36960-36970)
GIVEN
    `the amount of profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the compensation the partnership or limited liability partnership had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation that the partnership or limited liability partnership had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236G(6) the maximum recoverable amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the amount of profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided`) AND (`the amount of profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained` MINUS `the compensation the partnership or limited liability partnership had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN 0)
        THEN `the amount of profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained` MINUS `the compensation the partnership or limited liability partnership had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention`  -- FORK F-234-6: "(a) the profit gained; or (b) the loss avoided" read as the greater of the two when both are present
        IF (NOT (`the amount of profit that the partnership or limited liability partnership gained` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided`)) AND (`the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided` MINUS `the compensation the partnership or limited liability partnership had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN 0)
        THEN `the amount of the loss that the partnership or limited liability partnership avoided` MINUS `the compensation the partnership or limited liability partnership had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention`
        OTHERWISE 0  -- FORK F-234-6: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing recoverable


§ `s 236H: civil penalty against an officer of a corporation, a partner or manager, and the like`

-- src:36981 | 236H.—(1) Where it appears to the Authority that a corporation,
-- src:36982 | partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated
-- src:36983 | association (called in this section the contravening person) has
-- src:36984 | contravened any provision in this Part —
-- src:36986 | (a) with the consent or connivance of a person (called in this
-- src:36987 | section the defendant) who is an officer or (where its affairs
-- src:36988 | are managed by its members) a member of the corporation,
-- src:36989 | a partner of the partnership, a partner or manager of the
-- src:36990 | limited liability partnership, or an officer of the
-- src:36991 | unincorporated association (other than a partnership) or a
-- src:36992 | member of its governing body, as the case may be; or
-- src:36994 | (b) as a result of any neglect on the part of the defendant,
-- src:36996 | the Authority may, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an
-- src:36997 | action in a court against the defendant to seek an order for a civil
-- src:36998 | penalty in respect of that contravention as if the defendant had
-- src:36999 | committed the contravention, whether or not such action is brought
-- src:37000 | against the contravening person.
@ref s 236H(1) (src:36981-37000)
GIVEN
    `it appears to the Authority that the corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association has contravened a provision of Part 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it appear to the Authority that a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association (the contravening person) has contravened any provision in Part 12?
    `the person is an officer or member of the corporation, a partner of the partnership, a partner or manager of the limited liability partnership, or an officer or member of the governing body of the unincorporated association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an officer or (where its affairs are managed by its members) a member of the corporation, a partner of the partnership, a partner or manager of the limited liability partnership, or an officer of the unincorporated association (other than a partnership) or a member of its governing body, as the case may be?
    `the contravention was with the consent or connivance of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention with the consent or connivance of the person?
    `the contravention was as a result of neglect on the part of the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention as a result of any neglect on the part of the person?
    `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Public Prosecutor consented to the Authority bringing the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236H(1) the Authority may bring an action in a court against the defendant to seek an order for a civil penalty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`it appears to the Authority that the corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association has contravened a provision of Part 12` AND `the person is an officer or member of the corporation, a partner of the partnership, a partner or manager of the limited liability partnership, or an officer or member of the governing body of the unincorporated association` AND (`the contravention was with the consent or connivance of the person` OR `the contravention was as a result of neglect on the part of the person`))
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it appears to the Authority that a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association (called in this section the contravening person) has contravened any provision in this Part" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHERE] -- GRANT-GROUP [WHERE-LISTED]
        IF NOT `the Public Prosecutor has consented to the action`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Authority may, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, bring an action in a court against the defendant" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [CONSENT] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:37004 | (2) If the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the
-- src:37005 | contravening person has contravened a provision in this Part with the
-- src:37006 | consent or connivance of the defendant, or as a result of any neglect
-- src:37007 | on the part of the defendant, the court may make an order against the
-- src:37008 | defendant for the payment of a civil penalty of a sum not less than
-- src:37009 | $50,000 but not exceeding the greater of the following:
-- src:37011 | (a) 3 times —
-- src:37013 | (i) the amount of the profit that the defendant gained as
-- src:37014 | a result of the contravention by the contravening
-- src:37015 | person; or
-- src:37017 | (ii) the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided as a
-- src:37018 | result of the contravention by the contravening
-- src:37019 | person;
-- src:37021 | (b) $2 million.
@ref s 236H(2) (src:37004-37021)
GIVEN
    `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the contravening person contravened a provision of Part 12 with the consent or connivance of the defendant, or as a result of neglect on the part of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the contravening person has contravened a provision in Part 12 with the consent or connivance of the defendant, or as a result of any neglect on the part of the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236H(2) the court may make an order against the defendant for the payment of a civil penalty` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the contravening person contravened a provision of Part 12 with the consent or connivance of the defendant, or as a result of neglect on the part of the defendant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the contravening person has contravened a provision in this Part with the consent or connivance of the defendant" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [IF-NOTHING]


@ref s 236H(2) (src:37004-37021)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the profit that the defendant gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the profit that the defendant gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236H(2) the highest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (3 TIMES `the amount of the profit that the defendant gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`) GREATER THAN 2000000 AND `the amount of the profit that the defendant gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        THEN 3 TIMES `the amount of the profit that the defendant gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        IF (3 TIMES `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`) GREATER THAN 2000000
        THEN 3 TIMES `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`  -- FORK F-232-2a: "or" read as the greater of the two when both are present
        OTHERWISE 2000000  -- "not exceeding the greater of the following" (b) $2 million

@ref s 236H(2) (src:37004-37021)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236H(2) the lowest civil penalty the court may order` MEANS 50000  -- "a sum not less than $50,000"

-- s 236H(3) is shown as deleted in this text; the coverage table records it.

-- src:37030 | (4) Sections 232(4) to (7) and 233 apply in relation to an action
-- src:37031 | brought against a defendant under subsection (1) as they apply in
-- src:37032 | relation to an action under section 232.
@ref s 236H(4) (src:37030-37032)
GIVEN
    `the action is brought against the defendant under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action one brought against the defendant under subsection (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236H(4) sections 232(4) to (7) and 233 apply to the action under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the action is brought against the defendant under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply in relation to an action brought against a defendant under subsection (1)"

-- src:37036 | (5) Any defence that would be available to —
-- src:37038 | (a) the contravening person if it were prosecuted for its
-- src:37039 | contravention; or
-- src:37041 | (b) the defendant if he or she were prosecuted under
-- src:37042 | section 331 in respect of that contravention,
-- src:37044 | is also available to the defendant in an action under subsection (1) in
-- src:37045 | respect of that contravention.
@ref s 236H(5) (src:37036-37045)
GIVEN
    `a defence would be available to the contravening person if it were prosecuted for its contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the contravening person in a prosecution answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `a defence would be available to the defendant if he or she were prosecuted under section 331 in respect of that contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the defendant if he or she were prosecuted under section 331 in respect of that contravention answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236H(5) the defence is also available to the defendant in an action under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF (`a defence would be available to the contravening person if it were prosecuted for its contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`a defence would be available to the defendant if he or she were prosecuted under section 331 in respect of that contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is also available to the defendant in an action under subsection (1)"


§ `s 236I: civil liability of the defendant`

-- src:37051 | 236I.—(1) A defendant who has gained a profit or avoided a loss as
-- src:37052 | a result of the contravention of a provision in this Part by a
-- src:37053 | contravening person referred to in section 236H(1) is, whether or not
-- src:37054 | the defendant had been convicted under section 331 or had a civil
-- src:37055 | penalty imposed on the defendant under section 236H, liable to pay
-- src:37056 | compensation to any person (called in this section the claimant)
-- src:37057 | who —
-- src:37059 | (a) had been dealing in capital markets products of the same
-- src:37060 | description contemporaneously with the contravention by
-- src:37061 | the contravening person; and
-- src:37063 | (b) had suffered loss by reason of the difference between —
-- src:37065 | (i) the price at which the capital markets products were
-- src:37066 | dealt in contemporaneously with the contravention
-- src:37067 | by the contravening person; and
-- src:37069 | (ii) the price at which the capital markets products would
-- src:37070 | have been likely to have been so dealt in at the time
-- src:37071 | of the contemporaneous dealing if —
-- src:37073 | (A) in any case where the contravening person had
-- src:37074 | acted in contravention of section 218 or 219,
-- src:37079 | the information referred to in section 218(1) or
-- src:37080 | 219(1) (as the case may be) had been generally
-- src:37081 | available; or
-- src:37083 | (B) in any other case, the contravention by the
-- src:37084 | contravening person had not occurred.
@ref s 236I(1) (src:37051-37084)
GIVEN
    `the defendant is a defendant (the answer under section 236A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for "defendant" in section 236A answer for this defendant? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `the defendant has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the defendant gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention of a provision of Part 12 by the contravening person?
    `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person? (the court takes the matters in section 234(5) into account)
    `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price dealt in contemporaneously and the price likely to have been so dealt in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the claimant suffered loss by reason of the difference between (i) the price at which the capital markets products were dealt in contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person and (ii) the price at which they would have been likely to have been so dealt in, on the hypothesis that paragraph (b)(ii)(A) or (B) selects?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236I(1) the defendant is liable to pay compensation to the claimant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the defendant is a defendant (the answer under section 236A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A defendant who has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention of a provision in this Part by a contravening person referred to in section 236H(1)" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF NOT `the defendant has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b) -- GRANT-GROUP [ENTITLED]
        IF `the claimant had been dealing in capital markets products of the same description contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` AND `the claimant had suffered loss by reason of the difference between the price dealt in contemporaneously and the price likely to have been so dealt in`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any person (called in this section the claimant)" -- SPLIT-SITE (i) [OWN] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

@ref s 236I(1) (src:37073-37081)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the contravening person acted in contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236I(1)(b)(ii)(A) the price to compare is the price had the information been generally available` MEANS
    IF `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any case where the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219"

@ref s 236I(1) (src:37083-37084)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Had the contravening person acted in contravention of section 218 or 219?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236I(1)(b)(ii)(B) the price to compare is the price had the contravention not occurred` MEANS
    IF NOT `the contravening person had acted in contravention of section 218 or 219`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any other case"


-- src:37088 | (2) The amount of compensation that the defendant is liable to pay
-- src:37089 | to the claimant is the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant, after
-- src:37090 | deducting any amount of compensation paid or payable ––
-- src:37092 | (a) by the contravening person under an order of court or an
-- src:37093 | agreement to pay; or
-- src:37095 | (b) under an order for disgorgement under section 236L,
-- src:37097 | to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention, up to the
-- src:37098 | maximum recoverable amount.
@ref s 236I(2) (src:37088-37098)
GIVEN
    `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant?
    `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention under an order of court or an agreement to pay by the contravening person or any defendant, defendant corporation or defendant partnership under Division 4 or 5, or under an order for disgorgement under section 236L? (0 if none)
    `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 236I(6))` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the maximum recoverable amount under section 236I(6) for this contravention?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236I(2) the amount of compensation under subsection (1)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` AT MOST 0
        THEN 0  -- FORK F-234-2: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing owed
        IF `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 236I(6))`
        THEN `the maximum recoverable amount (the answer under section 236I(6))`  -- "up to the maximum recoverable amount"
        OTHERWISE `the amount of the loss suffered by the claimant` MINUS `the compensation paid or payable to the same claimant in respect of the same contravention`


-- src:37102 | (3) Any defence that would be available to —
-- src:37104 | (a) the contravening person if it were prosecuted for its
-- src:37105 | contravention; or
-- src:37107 | (b) the defendant if he or she were prosecuted under
-- src:37108 | section 331 in respect of that contravention,
-- src:37110 | is also available to the defendant in an action under this section in
-- src:37111 | respect of that contravention.
@ref s 236I(3) (src:37102-37111)
GIVEN
    `a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the contravening person in a prosecution answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
    `a defence would be available to the defendant if he or she were prosecuted under section 331 in respect of that contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question for the defence of the defendant if he or she were prosecuted under section 331 in respect of that contravention answer? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236I(3) the defence is also available to the defendant in an action under this section` MEANS
    IF (`a defence would be available to the contravening person if the contravening person were prosecuted for the contravening person's contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`a defence would be available to the defendant if he or she were prosecuted under section 331 in respect of that contravention (the answer under the section whose defence it is)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is also available to the defendant in an action under this section"


-- src:37115 | (4) An action under this section must not be commenced after the
-- src:37116 | expiration of 6 years from the date of completion of the
-- src:37117 | contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred.
@ref s 236I(4) (src:37115-37117)
GIVEN
    `the date of completion of the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred completed?
    `the date the action under section 236I is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the action under section 236I commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236I(4) the action under section 236I is barred because 6 years have expired from the date of completion of the dealing` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of completion of the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred` `the date the action under section 236I is commenced` 6 Years
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced after the expiration of 6 years from the date of completion of the contemporaneous dealing in which the loss occurred" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
    ELSE JUST TRUE


-- src:37121 | (5) In determining whether a dealing in capital markets products
-- src:37122 | took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the
-- src:37123 | contravening person, the court is to take into account the matters
-- src:37124 | referred to in section 234(5)(a) to (e).
@ref s 236I(5) (src:37121-37124)
GIVEN
    `the court is determining whether the dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court determining whether the dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236I(5) the court is to take into account the matters in section 234(5)` MEANS
    IF `the court is determining whether the dealing took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In determining whether" "took place contemporaneously with the contravention by the contravening person"


-- src:37128 | (6) In this section, “maximum recoverable amount” means —
-- src:37130 | (a) the amount of the profit that the defendant gained; or
-- src:37135 | (b) the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided,
-- src:37137 | as a result of the contravention by the contravening person, after
-- src:37138 | deducting all amounts of compensation that the defendant had
-- src:37139 | previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under
-- src:37140 | this section in respect of the same contravention.
@ref s 236I(6) (src:37128-37140)
GIVEN
    `the amount of profit that the defendant gained` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of profit that the defendant gained as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided as a result of the contravention by the contravening person? (0 if none)
    `the compensation the defendant had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of the compensation that the defendant had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236I(6) the maximum recoverable amount` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the amount of profit that the defendant gained` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided`) AND (`the amount of profit that the defendant gained` MINUS `the compensation the defendant had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN 0)
        THEN `the amount of profit that the defendant gained` MINUS `the compensation the defendant had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention`  -- FORK F-234-6: "(a) the profit gained; or (b) the loss avoided" read as the greater of the two when both are present
        IF (NOT (`the amount of profit that the defendant gained` GREATER THAN `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided`)) AND (`the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided` MINUS `the compensation the defendant had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention` GREATER THAN 0)
        THEN `the amount of the loss that the defendant avoided` MINUS `the compensation the defendant had previously been ordered by a court to pay to other claimants under this section in respect of the same contravention`
        OTHERWISE 0  -- FORK F-234-6: a negative result after deduction is read as nothing recoverable


§ `s 236J: actions not to commence or stayed in certain situations`

-- src:37148 | 236J.—(1) Except with the permission of court, no action may be
-- src:37149 | brought against —
-- src:37151 | (a) a defendant corporation under section 236B, 236C or
-- src:37152 | 236D;
-- src:37154 | (b) a defendant partnership (including, in the case of a
-- src:37155 | partnership, any of the partners) under section 236E,
-- src:37156 | 236F or 236G; or
-- src:37158 | (c) a defendant under section 236H or 236I,
-- src:37160 | which relates to a contravention of a provision in this Part (called in
-- src:37161 | this section the primary contravention) by a contravening person
-- src:37162 | referred to in section 236B(1) or 236C(1) (in relation to the defendant
-- src:37163 | corporation), 236E(1) or 236F(1) (in relation to the defendant
-- src:37164 | partnership) or 236H(1) (in relation to the defendant), as the case
-- src:37165 | may be, after the commencement of —
-- src:37167 | (d) criminal proceedings in respect of the primary
-- src:37168 | contravention against the contravening person; or
-- src:37170 | (e) an action under section 232 in respect of the primary
-- src:37171 | contravention against the contravening person,
@ref s 236J(1) (src:37148-37171)
GIVEN
    `the action is one against a defendant corporation, a defendant partnership or a defendant under section 236B, 236C, 236D, 236E, 236F, 236G, 236H or 236I which relates to a primary contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action one against a defendant corporation (section 236B, 236C or 236D), a defendant partnership (section 236E, 236F or 236G) or a defendant (section 236H or 236I) which relates to a contravention of a provision in Part 12 (the primary contravention) by the contravening person?
    `the action is brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings in respect of the primary contravention against the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings in respect of the primary contravention against the contravening person?
    `the action is brought after the commencement of an action under section 232 in respect of the primary contravention against the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action brought after the commencement of an action under section 232 in respect of the primary contravention against the contravening person?
    `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given permission for the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236J(1) no action against the defendant may be brought without the permission of court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is one against a defendant corporation, a defendant partnership or a defendant under section 236B, 236C, 236D, 236E, 236F, 236G, 236H or 236I which relates to a primary contravention`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no action may be brought against" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF NOT (`the action is brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings in respect of the primary contravention against the contravening person` OR `the action is brought after the commencement of an action under section 232 in respect of the primary contravention against the contravening person`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after the commencement of" -- MARGINAL-READING (b) -- FORK F-235-1: "after the commencement of" read as qualifying when the action is brought
        IF `the court has given permission`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except with the permission of court" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:37173 | and any such action in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) pending on the date of
-- src:37174 | commencement of the proceedings or action in paragraph (d) or (e)
-- src:37175 | must be stayed, and may not thereafter be continued except with the
-- src:37176 | permission of court.
@ref s 236J(1) (src:37173-37176)
GIVEN
    `the action is pending on the date of commencement of the criminal proceedings or of the action under section 232` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action pending on the date of commencement of the criminal proceedings in paragraph (d), or of the action under section 232 in paragraph (e)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236J(1) the pending action must be stayed` MEANS
    IF `the action is pending on the date of commencement of the criminal proceedings or of the action under section 232`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any such action in paragraph (a), (b) or (c) pending on the date of commencement" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

@ref s 236J(1) (src:37173-37176)
GIVEN
    `the action must be stayed (the answer under section 236J(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc The action must be stayed (the answer under section 236J(1)) (answer JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE, or NOTHING if it is not known)
    `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given permission for the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236J(1) the stayed action may thereafter be continued` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the action must be stayed (the answer under section 236J(1))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be stayed, and may not thereafter be continued except with the permission of court" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF `the court has given permission`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not thereafter be continued except with the permission of court"

-- src:37185 | (2) Permission under subsection (1) may not be granted if —
-- src:37187 | (a) in the criminal proceedings referred to in subsection (1)(d),
-- src:37188 | the contravening person has been acquitted of the primary
-- src:37189 | contravention; or
-- src:37191 | (b) in the action under section 232 referred to in
-- src:37192 | subsection (1)(e), the court is not satisfied that the
-- src:37193 | contravening person has committed the primary
-- src:37194 | contravention.
@ref s 236J(2) (src:37185-37194)
GIVEN
    `the contravening person has been acquitted of the primary contravention in the criminal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the criminal proceedings referred to in subsection (1)(d), has the contravening person been acquitted of the primary contravention?
    `the court is not satisfied in the action under section 232 that the contravening person has committed the primary contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the action under section 232 referred to in subsection (1)(e), is the court not satisfied that the contravening person has committed the primary contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236J(2) permission under subsection (1) may be granted` MEANS
    IF `the contravening person has been acquitted of the primary contravention in the criminal proceedings` OR `the court is not satisfied in the action under section 232 that the contravening person has committed the primary contravention`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Permission under subsection (1) may not be granted if"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not itself say when permission may be granted

-- src:37200 | (3) Except with the permission of court, no action
-- src:37201 | under section 236D, 236G or 236I may be brought against the
-- src:37202 | defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant in respect
-- src:37203 | of a primary contravention after the commencement of —
-- src:37205 | (a) criminal proceedings against the defendant corporation
-- src:37206 | under section 236B(1), the defendant partnership
-- src:37207 | (including, in the case of a partnership, any of the
-- src:37208 | partners) under section 236E(1) or the defendant under
-- src:37209 | section 331 in respect of the same contravention;
-- src:37211 | (b) an action against the defendant corporation under
-- src:37212 | section 236B(3), the defendant partnership under
-- src:37213 | section 236E(3) or the defendant under section 236H in
-- src:37214 | respect of the same contravention; or
-- src:37216 | (c) an action against the defendant corporation under
-- src:37217 | section 236C(2) or the defendant partnership under
-- src:37218 | section 236F(2) in respect of the failure to prevent or
-- src:37219 | detect that contravention,
@ref s 236J(3) (src:37200-37219)
GIVEN
    `the action is one under section 236D, 236G or 236I against the defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant in respect of a primary contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action one under section 236D, 236G or 236I against the defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant in respect of a primary contravention?
    `the action is brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings against the defendant under section 236B(1), 236E(1) or 331 in respect of the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings against the defendant corporation under section 236B(1), the defendant partnership (or, for a partnership, any of the partners) under section 236E(1) or the defendant under section 331 in respect of the same contravention?
    `the action is brought after the commencement of an action against the defendant under section 236B(3), 236E(3) or 236H in respect of the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action brought after the commencement of an action against the defendant corporation under section 236B(3), the defendant partnership under section 236E(3) or the defendant under section 236H in respect of the same contravention?
    `the action is brought after the commencement of an action under section 236C(2) or 236F(2) in respect of the failure to prevent or detect that contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action brought after the commencement of an action against the defendant corporation under section 236C(2) or the defendant partnership under section 236F(2) in respect of the failure to prevent or detect that contravention?
    `the court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the court given permission for the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236J(3) no action under section 236D, 236G or 236I may be brought without the permission of court` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the action is one under section 236D, 236G or 236I against the defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant in respect of a primary contravention`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no action under section 236D, 236G or 236I may be brought against the defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant in respect of a primary contravention" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF NOT (`the action is brought after the commencement of criminal proceedings against the defendant under section 236B(1), 236E(1) or 331 in respect of the same contravention` OR `the action is brought after the commencement of an action against the defendant under section 236B(3), 236E(3) or 236H in respect of the same contravention` OR `the action is brought after the commencement of an action under section 236C(2) or 236F(2) in respect of the failure to prevent or detect that contravention`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "after the commencement of" -- MARGINAL-READING (b) -- FORK F-235-1: "after the commencement of" read as qualifying when the action is brought
        IF `the court has given permission`
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except with the permission of court" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

