`s 236J(4) permission under subsection (3) may be granted` MEANS
    IF `a date has been fixed by a court under section 236K for the filing of claims`
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Permission under subsection (3) may not be granted if a date has been fixed by a court under section 236K for the filing of claims"
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not itself say when permission may be granted

@ref s 236J(4) (src:37230-37239)
GIVEN
    `the number of days the court's directions allow for the filing and proof of the claim` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many days do the directions that the court issues in the claimant's case require the claim to be filed and proved?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 236A to s 236L duty`
`s 236J(4) the claimant must comply with the court's directions on the filing and proof of the claim` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the claimant"
    MUST `s 236J(4) comply with the court's directions on the filing and proof of the claim under section 236K`
    WITHIN `the number of days the court's directions allow for the filing and proof of the claim`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the claimant did not file and prove the claim within the time the court's directions allow (section 236J(4))"


§ `s 236K: civil liability in event of conviction or civil penalty`

-- src:37247 | 236K.—(1) Despite section 236D, 236G or 236I, where a
-- src:37248 | defendant corporation, defendant partnership (including, in the case
-- src:37249 | of a partnership, any of the partners) or defendant —
-- src:37251 | (a) has been convicted of an offence under this Division; or
-- src:37253 | (b) has had an order for the payment of civil penalty made
-- src:37254 | against it, him or her under this Division, other than by way
-- src:37255 | of a default judgment or a consent order made with or
-- src:37256 | without admission of contravention,
-- src:37258 | and has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the
-- src:37259 | contravention by the contravening person referred to in
-- src:37260 | section 236B(1), 236C(1), 236E(1), 236F(1) or 236H(1) (as the
-- src:37261 | case may be) the court which convicted or made the order for a civil
-- src:37262 | penalty against the defendant corporation, defendant partnership (or
-- src:37263 | any of the partners thereof) or defendant may, after the conviction or
-- src:37264 | the order imposing the civil penalty has been made final, fix a date on
-- src:37265 | or before which all claimants have to file and prove their claims
-- src:37266 | against the defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant
-- src:37267 | (as the case may be) for compensation in respect of that
-- src:37268 | contravention.
@ref s 236K(1) (src:37247-37268)
GIVEN
    `the defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant has been convicted of an offence under Division 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the defendant corporation, defendant partnership (or, for a partnership, any of the partners) or defendant been convicted of an offence under Division 5?
    `an order for the payment of a civil penalty has been made against it, him or her under Division 5, other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order for the payment of a civil penalty been made against it, him or her under Division 5, other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order made with or without admission of contravention?
    `it, he or she has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it, he or she gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person referred to in section 236B(1), 236C(1), 236E(1), 236F(1) or 236H(1)?
    `the conviction or the order has been made final (the answer under section 236(4) or (5) as applied by section 236K(2))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 236(4) (conviction) or section 236(5) (order), as applied by section 236K(2), answer? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236K(1) the court may fix a date on or before which all claimants have to file and prove their claims` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT ((`the defendant corporation, defendant partnership or defendant has been convicted of an offence under Division 5` OR `an order for the payment of a civil penalty has been made against it, him or her under Division 5, other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order`) AND `it, he or she has gained a profit or avoided a loss as a result of the contravention by the contravening person`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a defendant corporation, defendant partnership" "has been convicted of an offence under this Division" "other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHERE] -- GRANT-GROUP [WHERE-LISTED]
        IF NOT (`the conviction or the order has been made final (the answer under section 236(4) or (5) as applied by section 236K(2))` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may, after the conviction or the order imposing the civil penalty has been made final, fix a date" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [AFTER] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:37272 | (2) Section 236(2) to (5) applies, with the necessary modifications,
-- src:37273 | to an action under subsection (1), and in such application —
@ref s 236K(2) (src:37272-37273)
