§ `s 236L: order for disgorgement against a third party`

-- src:37300 | 236L.—(1) Without affecting any action under section 234, 236,
-- src:37301 | 236D, 236G, 236I or 236K, where —
-- src:37303 | (a) a person has been convicted by a court of an offence in
-- src:37304 | respect of a contravention of any provision in this Part;
-- src:37306 | (b) a person has had an order for the payment of a civil penalty
-- src:37307 | made against the person under section 232 or any of the
-- src:37308 | provisions in this Division by a court, other than by way of
-- src:37309 | a default judgment or a consent order made with or without
-- src:37310 | admission of contravention, in respect of a contravention
-- src:37311 | of any provision in this Part; or
-- src:37313 | (c) in an action commenced under this section, a court is
-- src:37314 | satisfied on a balance of probabilities that a contravention
-- src:37315 | by a person of any provision in this Part has occurred,
-- src:37317 | the court may, on the application of the Authority or any claimant,
-- src:37318 | make an order against any other person (called in this section a third
-- src:37319 | party) who has received the whole or any part of the benefit of that
-- src:37320 | contravention for disgorgement of that benefit, being benefit derived
-- src:37321 | from trades carried out for the third party by the person referred to in
-- src:37322 | paragraph (a), (b) or (c).
@ref s 236L(1) (src:37300-37322)
GIVEN
    `a person has been convicted by a court of an offence in respect of a contravention of a provision of Part 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person been convicted by a court of an offence in respect of a contravention of any provision in Part 12?
    `a person has had an order for the payment of a civil penalty made against the person under section 232 or Division 5, other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a person had an order for the payment of a civil penalty made against the person under section 232 or any of the provisions in Division 5 by a court, other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order made with or without admission of contravention, in respect of a contravention of any provision in Part 12?
    `in an action commenced under section 236L a court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that a contravention of a provision of Part 12 by a person has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In an action commenced under section 236L, is a court satisfied on a balance of probabilities that a contravention by a person of any provision in Part 12 has occurred?
    `the Authority or a claimant has applied for the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority or any claimant applied for the order?
    `the other person has received the whole or any part of the benefit of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other person (the third party) received the whole or any part of the benefit of that contravention?
    `the benefit was derived from trades carried out for the third party by the person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the benefit one derived from trades carried out for the third party by the person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(1) the court may make an order against the third party for disgorgement of the benefit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a person has been convicted by a court of an offence in respect of a contravention of a provision of Part 12` OR `a person has had an order for the payment of a civil penalty made against the person under section 232 or Division 5, other than by way of a default judgment or a consent order` OR `in an action commenced under section 236L a court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that a contravention of a provision of Part 12 by a person has occurred`)
        THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where" "a person has been convicted by a court of an offence in respect of a contravention of any provision in this Part" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHERE] -- GRANT-GROUP [WHERE-LISTED]
        IF NOT `the Authority or a claimant has applied for the order`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court may, on the application of the Authority or any claimant, make an order" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [APPLICATION] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF NOT (`the other person has received the whole or any part of the benefit of the contravention` AND `the benefit was derived from trades carried out for the third party by the person referred to in paragraph (a), (b) or (c)`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against any other person (called in this section a third party) who has received the whole or any part of the benefit of that contravention" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHO] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:37326 | (2) The court must issue a notice to a third party against whom an
-- src:37327 | application for an order for disgorgement under subsection (1) is
-- src:37328 | made, giving the third party an opportunity to show cause, within
-- src:37329 | such time as may be specified in the notice, why the order should not
-- src:37330 | be made.
@ref s 236L(2) (src:37326-37330)
GIVEN
    `an application for an order for disgorgement has been made against the third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for an order for disgorgement under subsection (1) been made against the third party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(2) the third party is to be given notice and an opportunity to show cause why the order should not be made` MEANS
    IF `an application for an order for disgorgement has been made against the third party`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against whom an application for an order for disgorgement under subsection (1) is made"

-- src:37337 | (3) An application for an order for disgorgement under
-- src:37338 | subsection (1) must not be commenced after the expiration of
-- src:37339 | 6 years from the date on which the contravention referred to in that
-- src:37340 | subsection was committed.
@ref s 236L(3) (src:37337-37340)
GIVEN
    `the date on which the contravention was committed` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the contravention referred to in section 236L(1) committed?
    `the date the application for an order for disgorgement is commenced` IS A DATE @desc On what date is the application for an order for disgorgement commenced?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(3) the application for an order for disgorgement is barred because 6 years have expired from the date of the contravention` MEANS
    IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date on which the contravention was committed` `the date the application for an order for disgorgement is commenced` 6 Years
    THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be commenced after the expiration of 6 years from the date on which the contravention referred to in that subsection was committed" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:37344 | (4) The court is not to make an order for disgorgement against a
-- src:37345 | third party, or is not to order disgorgement of the entire benefit
-- src:37346 | derived by the third party, if the court is satisfied, on a balance of
-- src:37347 | probabilities, that —
-- src:37349 | (a) the third party acquired the benefit without knowing, and
-- src:37350 | in circumstances such as not to arouse a reasonable
-- src:37351 | suspicion, that the benefit was derived from the
-- src:37352 | contravention referred to in subsection (1); and
-- src:37354 | (b) the third party has so altered the third party’s position in
-- src:37355 | reliance on the third party having an indefeasible interest in
-- src:37356 | the benefit that, in the opinion of the court, it would be
-- src:37357 | inequitable to make the order for disgorgement or to order
-- src:37358 | disgorgement of the entire benefit derived by the third
-- src:37359 | party, as the case may be.
@ref s 236L(4) (src:37344-37359)
GIVEN
    `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the third party acquired the benefit without knowing, and in circumstances such as not to arouse a reasonable suspicion, that it was derived from the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the third party acquired the benefit without knowing, and in circumstances such as not to arouse a reasonable suspicion, that the benefit was derived from the contravention referred to in subsection (1)?
    `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the third party has so altered its position in reliance on an indefeasible interest in the benefit that it would be inequitable to make the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the court satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that the third party has so altered the third party's position in reliance on the third party having an indefeasible interest in the benefit that, in the opinion of the court, it would be inequitable to make the order for disgorgement, or to order disgorgement of the entire benefit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(4) the court is not to make an order for disgorgement, or not of the entire benefit, against the third party` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the third party acquired the benefit without knowing, and in circumstances such as not to arouse a reasonable suspicion, that it was derived from the contravention` AND `the court is satisfied on a balance of probabilities that the third party has so altered its position in reliance on an indefeasible interest in the benefit that it would be inequitable to make the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the court is satisfied, on a balance of probabilities, that" -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- this section gives no relief on these facts

-- src:37363 | (5) Despite subsection (4), the court may make an order for
-- src:37364 | disgorgement against a third party referred to in subsection (4) of a
-- src:37365 | sum that is, in the opinion of the court, equitable.
@ref s 236L(5) (src:37363-37365)
GIVEN
    `the third party is a third party referred to in subsection (4) (the answer under section 236L(4))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 236L(4) answer for this third party? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(5) the court may make an order for disgorgement against the third party of a sum that is equitable` MEANS
    IF `the third party is a third party referred to in subsection (4) (the answer under section 236L(4))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against a third party referred to in subsection (4) of a sum that is, in the opinion of the court, equitable" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHO] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

-- src:37369 | (6) The court may, after the order for disgorgement has been made
-- src:37370 | final, fix a date, not earlier than 6 months from the date the order for
-- src:37371 | disgorgement has been made final, on or before which all claimants
-- src:37372 | have to file and prove their claims for compensation in respect of the
-- src:37373 | contravention referred to in subsection (1).
@ref s 236L(6) (src:37369-37373)
GIVEN
    `the order for disgorgement has been made final (the answer under section 236L(11))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 236L(11) answer for the order for disgorgement? (JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(6) the court may fix a date on or before which all claimants have to file and prove their claims` MEANS
    IF `the order for disgorgement has been made final (the answer under section 236L(11))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may, after the order for disgorgement has been made final, fix a date" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [AFTER] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

@ref s 236L(6) (src:37369-37373)
GIVEN
    `the date the order for disgorgement was made final` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the order for disgorgement made final?
    `the date the court fixes for the filing and proof of claims` IS A DATE @desc What date does the court fix for the filing and proof of claims?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(6) the date fixed is not earlier than 6 months from the date the order for disgorgement was made final` MEANS
    IF `the date the court fixes for the filing and proof of claims` AT LEAST `period: the last day of a period after` `the date the order for disgorgement was made final` 6 Months
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "fix a date, not earlier than 6 months from the date the order for disgorgement has been made final"

-- src:37377 | (7) The court may, after the expiry of the date fixed under
-- src:37378 | subsection (6), order that each claimant who has filed and proven
-- src:37379 | the claimant’s claim for compensation be paid out of the sum under
-- src:37380 | the final order for disgorgement, an amount —
@ref s 236L(7) (src:37377-37380)
GIVEN
    `the date fixed under section 236L(6) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the date fixed under section 236L(6) expired?
    `the claimant has filed and proven the claimant's claim for compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the claimant filed and proven the claimant's claim for compensation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(7) the court may order that the claimant be paid out of the sum under the final order for disgorgement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the date fixed under section 236L(6) has expired`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may, after the expiry of the date fixed under subsection (6), order" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [AFTER] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        IF NOT `the claimant has filed and proven the claimant's claim for compensation`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each claimant who has filed and proven the claimant’s claim for compensation" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [WHO] -- MARGINAL-READING (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:37382 | (a) equal to the amount of loss suffered by the claimant, after
-- src:37383 | deducting any other compensation paid or payable to the
-- src:37388 | same claimant under an order of court or an agreement to
-- src:37389 | pay in respect of the same contravention; or
-- src:37391 | (b) equal to the pro‑rated portion of the sum under the final
-- src:37392 | order for disgorgement, calculated according to the
-- src:37393 | relationship which the amount referred to in
-- src:37394 | paragraph (a) bears to all amounts proved to the court,
-- src:37396 | whichever is the lesser.
@ref s 236L(7) (src:37382-37396)
GIVEN
    `the amount of loss suffered by the claimant after deducting any other compensation paid or payable to the same claimant` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of loss suffered by the claimant, after deducting any other compensation paid or payable to the same claimant under an order of court or an agreement to pay in respect of the same contravention?
    `the sum under the final order for disgorgement` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum under the final order for disgorgement?
    `all amounts proved to the court` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total of all amounts proved to the court (the amount in paragraph (a) for every claimant, this claimant's included)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236L(7) the amount to be paid to the claimant out of the sum under the final order for disgorgement` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `all amounts proved to the court` AT MOST 0
        THEN 0  -- FORK F-236L-7: nothing is proved, so nothing is paid
        IF `the amount of loss suffered by the claimant after deducting any other compensation paid or payable to the same claimant` AT MOST (`the sum under the final order for disgorgement` TIMES `the amount of loss suffered by the claimant after deducting any other compensation paid or payable to the same claimant` DIVIDED BY `all amounts proved to the court`)
        THEN `the amount of loss suffered by the claimant after deducting any other compensation paid or payable to the same claimant`  -- "whichever is the lesser"
        OTHERWISE `the sum under the final order for disgorgement` TIMES `the amount of loss suffered by the claimant after deducting any other compensation paid or payable to the same claimant` DIVIDED BY `all amounts proved to the court`  -- "all amounts proved to the court" has no "other", so the claimant's own amount is in the total (contrast section 236(3A)(b))

-- src:37400 | (8) Any sum remaining under the order for disgorgement must be
-- src:37401 | paid into the Consolidated Fund and is to be treated as a debt due to
-- src:37402 | the Government for the purposes of section 10 of the Government
-- src:37403 | Proceedings Act 1956.
@ref s 236L(8) (src:37400-37403)
GIVEN
    `the sum under the order for disgorgement` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number: the sum under the order for disgorgement?
    `the total paid out to claimants under the order` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total paid out to claimants under the order for disgorgement?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 236L(8) the sum remaining under the order to be paid into the Consolidated Fund` MEANS
    IF `the sum under the order for disgorgement` MINUS `the total paid out to claimants under the order` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the sum under the order for disgorgement` MINUS `the total paid out to claimants under the order`

-- src:37407 | (9) If the third party fails to pay the sums under the order for
-- src:37408 | disgorgement within the time specified in the court order under
-- src:37409 | subsection (7) ––
-- src:37411 | (a) each claimant may recover the sum due to the claimant
-- src:37412 | under the order for disgorgement as though it were a
-- src:37413 | judgment debt due to the claimant; and
@ref s 236L(9) (src:37407-37413)
GIVEN
    `the third party fails to pay the sums under the order for disgorgement within the time specified in the court order under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the third party fail to pay the sums under the order for disgorgement within the time specified in the court order under subsection (7)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(9)(a) each claimant may recover the sum due as though it were a judgment debt due to the claimant` MEANS
    IF `the third party fails to pay the sums under the order for disgorgement within the time specified in the court order under subsection (7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "each claimant may recover the sum due to the claimant under the order for disgorgement" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [IF-NOTHING]

@ref s 236L(9) (src:37407-37413)
GIVEN
    `the number of days the court order under subsection (7) allows for payment` IS A NUMBER @desc Within how many days does the court order under section 236L(7) require the third party to pay the sums under the order for disgorgement?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 236A to s 236L duty`
`s 236L(9) the third party must pay the sums under the order for disgorgement within the time specified in the court order` MEANS
    PARTY Individual "the third party"
    MUST `s 236L(9) pay the sums under the order for disgorgement`
    WITHIN `the number of days the court order under subsection (7) allows for payment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BECAUSE "the third party did not pay the sums under the order for disgorgement within the time specified in the court order under section 236L(7) (section 236L(9))"

-- src:37415 | (b) the remaining sum under the order for disgorgement may
-- src:37416 | be recovered by the Authority as though it were a judgment
-- src:37417 | debt due to the Authority and paid into the Consolidated
-- src:37418 | Fund.
@ref s 236L(9) (src:37415-37418)
GIVEN
    `the third party fails to pay the sums under the order for disgorgement within the time specified in the court order under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the third party fail to pay the sums under the order for disgorgement within the time specified in the court order under subsection (7)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(9)(b) the Authority may recover the remaining sum as though it were a judgment debt due to the Authority` MEANS
    IF `the third party fails to pay the sums under the order for disgorgement within the time specified in the court order under subsection (7)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the remaining sum under the order for disgorgement may be recovered by the Authority" -- SPLIT-SITE (ii) [IF] -- MARGINAL-READING (a) -- GRANT-GROUP [IF-NOTHING]

-- src:37422 | (10) After the expiry of the date fixed under subsection (6), no
-- src:37423 | person may make any subsequent application under this section for an
-- src:37424 | order for disgorgement against the third party in respect of the same
-- src:37425 | contravention.
@ref s 236L(10) (src:37422-37425)
GIVEN
    `the date fixed under section 236L(6) has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the date fixed under section 236L(6) expired?
    `the application is for an order for disgorgement against the same third party in respect of the same contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one for an order for disgorgement against the same third party in respect of the same contravention?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(10) no subsequent application for an order for disgorgement may be made against the third party` MEANS
    IF `the date fixed under section 236L(6) has expired` AND `the application is for an order for disgorgement against the same third party in respect of the same contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "After the expiry of the date fixed under subsection (6), no person may make any subsequent application" -- MARGINAL-READING (b)

-- src:37429 | (11) For the purposes of this section, an order for disgorgement is
-- src:37430 | made final if —
-- src:37432 | (a) the order is not set aside on appeal or revision or is varied
-- src:37433 | only as to the sum to be disgorged;
-- src:37435 | (b) the order is not subject to further appeal;
-- src:37440 | (c) no notice of appeal against the order is lodged within the
-- src:37441 | time prescribed by Rules of Court; or
-- src:37443 | (d) any appeal against the order is withdrawn. [2/2009]
@ref s 236L(11) (src:37429-37443)
GIVEN
    `the order is not set aside on appeal or revision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order not set aside on appeal or revision?
    `the order is varied only as to the sum to be disgorged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order varied only as to the sum to be disgorged?
    `the order is not subject to further appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order not subject to further appeal?
    `no notice of appeal against the order is lodged within the time prescribed by Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no notice of appeal against the order is lodged within the time prescribed by Rules of Court? (the Rules are not among the sources)
    `any appeal against the order is withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that any appeal against the order is withdrawn?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(11) the order for disgorgement is made final` MEANS
    IF `the order is not set aside on appeal or revision` OR `the order is varied only as to the sum to be disgorged` OR `the order is not subject to further appeal` OR `no notice of appeal against the order is lodged within the time prescribed by Rules of Court` OR `any appeal against the order is withdrawn`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an order for disgorgement is made final if" -- MARGINAL-READING (a)

-- src:37444 | (12) In this section —
-- src:37446 | “benefit”, in relation to a contravention of any provision in this
-- src:37447 | Part, means a profit gained or loss avoided as a result of that
-- src:37448 | contravention;
@ref s 236L(12) (src:37444-37448)
GIVEN
    `the thing is a profit gained or loss avoided as a result of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the thing a profit gained, or a loss avoided, as a result of the contravention of a provision in Part 12?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(12) "benefit" a profit gained or loss avoided as a result of the contravention` MEANS
    IF `the thing is a profit gained or loss avoided as a result of the contravention`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“benefit”, in relation to a contravention of any provision in this Part, means a profit gained or loss avoided as a result of that contravention"

-- src:37450 | “claimant”, in relation to a contravention of any provision in this
-- src:37451 | Part, means any person who would qualify as a claimant
-- src:37452 | under section 234 in respect of that contravention.
@ref s 236L(12) (src:37450-37452)
GIVEN
    `the person would qualify as a claimant under section 234 in respect of the contravention (the answer under section 234(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the question under section 234(1) answer for this person in respect of the contravention? (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 236L(12) "claimant" a person who would qualify as a claimant under section 234` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person would qualify as a claimant under section 234 in respect of the contravention (the answer under section 234(1))` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person would qualify as a claimant under section 234 in respect of the contravention (the answer under section 234(1))` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person qualifies under section 234 was not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“claimant”, in relation to a contravention of any provision in this Part, means any person who would qualify as a claimant under section 234 in respect of that contravention"

DECLARE `s 236A to s 236L duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 236J(4) comply with the court's directions on the filing and proof of the claim under section 236K`
    `s 236L(9) pay the sums under the order for disgorgement`

§ `s 237: jurisdiction of District Court`

-- src:37462 | 237. A District Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine any
-- src:37463 | action or application under Division 4 or 5 regardless of the monetary
-- src:37464 | amount.
@ref s 237 (src:37462-37464)
GIVEN
    `the action or application is under Division 4 or 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action or application one under Division 4 or Division 5 of Part 12?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 237 a District Court has jurisdiction to hear and determine the action or application regardless of the monetary amount` MEANS
    IF `the action or application is under Division 4 or 5`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to hear and determine any action or application under Division 4 or 5"

